---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: stdout(&output)
---
tokendraw findings, all calls

fixed-context
  Each call re-read on average 4,840 tokens its session started with: the
  system prompt, tool definitions, instruction files and first prompt. That
  used 81% of the energy.
  What you can do:
    claude-code: /context to see what fills the context, /mcp disable for
    servers you do not use, /memory to shorten CLAUDE.md
    codex: enabled = false in config.toml for MCP servers you do not use,
    shorten AGENTS.md
    pi: /mcp to disable servers you do not use, shorten AGENTS.md
  To see the effect, run this after the change:
  `tokendraw findings --since <tomorrow>`

long-context
  No calls carried more than 200,000 cached tokens.
